l":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Eukaryotes are larger than prokaryotes"},{"label":"B","text":"Prokaryotes have no nuclear membrane"},{"label":"C","text":"Eukaryotes have a diploid genome and prokaryotes have a haploid genome"},{"label":"D","text":"Prokaryotes have cytoplasm rich in 70S ribosomes"},{"label":"E","text":"Eukaryotes and prokaryotes reproduce sexually and have cell walls"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1a709b1fbafc","stem":"In general, Gram-negative bacteria are more pathogenic and Gram-positive bacteria are more susceptible to β-lactam antibiotics such as penicillin. Which of the following best describes the steps, in order, of Gram staining for peptidoglycan?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Apply crystal violet stain => Add mordant => Add alcohol or acetone => Counterstain with safranin or basic fuchin"},{"label":"B","text":"Apply mordant stain => Add crystal violet => Add alcohol or acetone => Counterstain with safranin or basic fuchin"},{"label":"C","text":"Apply crystal violet stain => Add alcohol or acetone => Add mordant => Counterstain with safranin or basic fuchin"},{"label":"D","text":"Apply safranin or basic fuchin stain => Add mordant => Add alcohol or acetone => Counterstain with crystal violet"},{"label":"E","text":"Apply safranin or basic fuchin stain => Add alcohol or acetone => Add mordant => Counterstain with crystal violet"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"ke