 b) Viral glycoprotein; c) Hemagglutinin (HA)"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-97553aa2722a","stem":"RNA-dependent RNA polymerase (RDRP) associates with the (____) RNA genome of the orthomyxoviruses, paramyxoviruses, and rhabdoviruses to form helical nucleocapsids and uses ____ as a template.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"+; RNA"},{"label":"B","text":"-; RNA"},{"label":"C","text":"+; DNA"},{"label":"D","text":"-; DNA"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_text","prior_structural_review_flag"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0777c9b5b180","stem":"Which of the following is NOT true regarding Influenza A (orthomyxovirus)?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is a (-) RNA virus"},{"label":"B","text":"It has a segmented genome"},{"label":"C","text":"It has the glycoprotein hemagglutinin (HA)"},{"label":"D","text":"It has the glycoprotein neuraminidase (NA)"},{"label":"E","text":"Like bunyaviruses, it does n