iology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bacteremia"},{"label":"B","text":"Endocarditis"},{"label":"C","text":"Breast abscess"},{"label":"D","text":"Urinary tract infection"},{"label":"E","text":"Wound infection"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-22eb4c0cc665","stem":"2) Which of the following is NOT a common disease caused by Abiotrophia sp.?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Eye infection"},{"label":"B","text":"Oral infection"},{"label":"C","text":"Endocarditis"},{"label":"D","text":"Urinary tract infection"},{"label":"E","text":"Bacteremia"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-279f2f131c37","stem":"Vancomycin-resistant enterococci (VRE) are troublesome because the resistance is mediated by which of the following, allowing it to be transferred to other bacteria?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Flagellum"},{"label":"B","text":"Ribosomes"},{"label":"C","text":"Cytoplasm"},{"label":