obic; Aerobic and facultative anaerobic"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"independent_no_source_key_bulk_v4","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"bc8be1e692641309aa75e3b30384eb51dd9f4e28"},{"id":"q-5bda02cff21e","stem":"1) Which of the following is/are the toxic form(s) of proteins on the large plasmid (virulence factor) of B. anthracis, which lead to the damage of a large range of tissues?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Protective antigen (PA) - binds cell membranes"},{"label":"B","text":"Edema factor (EF) - adenylate cyclase activity"},{"label":"C","text":"Lethal factor (LF) - causes cell death"},{"label":"D","text":"PA + EF + LF"},{"label":"E","text":"PA + EF and PA + LF"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-566f256cf80e","stem":"2) Which of the following is a virulence factor of B. anthracis that inhibits phagocytosis of replicating cells?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"M Protein"},{"label":"B","text":"O polysaccharide"},{"la