olate worldwide"},{"label":"E","text":"Spores can easily be prepared from liquid cultures Match the following resulting biological effect with their form of anthrax:"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d24d7dd7bc92","stem":"A young man enters the Emergency Room dehydrated, afebrile, and complaining of nausea and vomiting. Since he began vomiting one hour ago, he has been “hugging the toilet” nearly every ten minutes. He remembers eating a dish with fried rice at an Asian restaurant several hours ago. Which of the following is most likely the cause?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"C. tetani"},{"label":"B","text":"C. botulinum"},{"label":"C","text":"C. difficile"},{"label":"D","text":"B. anthracis"},{"label":"E","text":"B. cereus 26 – Listeria"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-46110014d0de","stem":"Which of the following is NOT a useful feature in identifying Listeria?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Facultative anaerobe coccobacilli often arranged in pairs"},{"label":"B","text":"Only Gram-positive bacteria with an endotoxin"},{"label":"C","text":"Motile at room temperature"},{"label":"D","text":"γ-hemolytic (non-hemolytic)"},{"label":"E","text":"Capable of growth in high-salt concentrations"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option B"],"duplicateStemGroup":"530d519b1a5860296e69a1d0a894e50031c6d0b1"},{"id":"q-0882b802d085","stem":"1) A mother brings her 2-month-old infant to the hospital because he exhibits fever, convulsions, irritability, and poor eating. The pediatrician-in-training notes a widespread rash and a stiff neck on physical exam. She orders a spinal tap, which reveals low glucose, increased PMNs, increased proteins, and Gram-positive rode with “tumbling” motility in cultures. Upon further questioning, the pediatrician discovers that the mother does not breast feed and feeds her baby fresh cow milk. Which of the following is the most likely cause?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"C. diphtheriae"},{"label":"B","text":"S. pneumoniae"},{"label":"C","text":"S. aureus"},{"label":"D","text":"L. monocytogenes"},{"label":"E","text":"S. pyogenes"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0248c475e8a5",