:"3) Which of the following produces heat-labile (LT-I and LT-II) and heat-stabile (STa and STb) enterotoxins that stimulate hypersecretion of fluids and electrolytes?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Vibrio cholerae"},{"label":"B","text":"EHEC"},{"label":"C","text":"Shigella dysenteriae"},{"label":"D","text":"ETEC"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-289994d815ab","stem":"4) Which of the following interacts with G proteins that control adenylate cyclase, leading to the catabolic conversion of adenosine triphosphate (ATP) to cyclic adenosine monophosphate (cAMP), resulting in a hypersecretion of water and electrolytes?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Vibrio cholerae"},{"label":"B","text":"EHEC"},{"label":"C","text":"Shigella dysenteriae"},{"label":"D","text":"ETEC"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"6048d1faed5b0d98d202c9c0a84e8815839fbcd1"},{"id":"q-70b2aa7571b4","stem":"What virulence factor of E. coli is associated with adhesion in the urinary and gastrointestinal tracts and also binds to a blood group antigen?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Colonizing factor antigens"},{"label":"B","text":"Aggregative adherence fimbriae"},{"label":"C","text":"P. pili"},{"label":"D","text":"Intimin"},{"label":"E","text":"Ipa protein Use the following key (a-f) to match the bacteria to the illness it causes:"},{"label":"A","text":"Salmonella typhi"},{"label":"B","text":"Salmonella enteritidis"},{"label":"C","text":"Shigella dysenteriae"},{"label":"D","text":"Yersinia enterocolitica"},{"label":"E","text":"Yersinia pestis"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7a296f6c0b2d","stem":"1) A photographer for National Geographic returning from Thailand develops a fever and abdominal cramps on the plane. By the time the plane lands, he suffers from bloody diarrhea. His fever peaks at 40oC. The doctor decides to do an endoscopy exam and makes a diagnosis based on the hemorrhagic mucosa and ulcerations observed in the distal colon. Which of the options is the most likely cause?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":f