tice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-e82be3986726","stem":"4) A man and his two sons just returned from a vacation on their relative’s farm. All three arrived complaining of bloody diarrhea. The youngest son becomes well spontaneously. The older son complains of right flank pain, while the father starts to notice tenderness in his joints. One surgeon, worried about appendicitis in the older son, performs the initial incision and discovers a normal appendix but an inflamed colon. After also observing swollen mesenteric lymph nodes during surgery, he makes a diagnosis explaining the symptoms in all 3 patients. Which of the options is the most likely cause?","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Abdominal Surgery · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Abdominal Surgery","options":[],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Abdominal Surgery · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-daa17af20048","stem":"6) Which of the following is NOT a route of transmission for Shigella dysenteriae?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fingers"},{"label":"B","text":"Flies"},{"label":"C","text":"Farms"},{"label":"D","text":"Food"},{"label":"E","text":"Feces"}],"prior