demic outbreaks can occur in daycare centers and nurseries"},{"label":"D","text":"Primary transmission is by people with contaminated hands"},{"label":"E","text":"Spreads rapidly even in communities where sanitary standards are high"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4b24b4939158","stem":"1) Which of the following is the natural reservoir for urban plague (Y. pestis)?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cows"},{"label":"B","text":"Rabbits"},{"label":"C","text":"Turtles"},{"label":"D","text":"Rats"},{"label":"E","text":"Mosquitoes"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-745dcc7e5e3e","stem":"2) Which of the following is NOT a natural reservoir for sylvatic plague (Y. pestis)?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Squirrels"},{"label":"B","text":"Rabbits"},{"label":"C","text":"Livestock"},{"label":"D","text":"Rats"},{"label":"E","text":"Domestic cats"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option B"],"duplicateStemGroup":"77355044852d1088b9b462b6b15cadb169b2157b"},{"id":"q-4bdef4a6368f","stem":"Bubonic plagues (Y. pestis) is characterized by ____ and pneumonic plague (Y. pestis) is characterized by ____.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"A 7-day incubation period; A 3-day incubation period"},{"label":"B","text":"A > 90% mortality rate; A >75% mortality rate"},{"label":"C","text":"Pulmonary disease; A painful bubo (inflammation of the lymph nodes)"},{"label":"D","text":"Aerosol spreading from person-to-person; Flea bites"},{"label":"E","text":"Septicemia; Cutaneous hemorrhagic necrosis 32 – Vibrios"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f73b37696a6c","stem":"Aside from the presence of polar flagella, which of the following laboratory tests can differentiate Vibrionaceae from Enterobacteriaceae?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Oxidase reaction"},{"label":"B","text":"Urease reaction"},{"label":"C","text":"Glucose/Dextrose fermentation"},{"label":"D","text":"Sucrose fermentation"},{"label":"E","text":"Lactose reaction"}],"prio