 bacteria?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Microscopy"},{"label":"B","text":"Urease test"},{"label":"C","text":"Antigen detection"},{"label":"D","text":"Culture"},{"label":"E","text":"Serology"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d690822f37c1","stem":"2) Which of the following laboratory test for H. pylori requires a biopsy and identifies the bacteria if the result is positive?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Microscopy"},{"label":"B","text":"Urease test"},{"label":"C","text":"Antigen detection"},{"label":"D","text":"Culture"},{"label":"E","text":"Serology"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-102f9ef82532","stem":"The greatest success in curing gastritis or peptic ulcer disease has been accomplished with the combination of antibiotics and which of the following?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antibiotic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Proton pump inhibitor (PPI)"},{"label":"B","tex