q-ec8ba7088413","stem":"5) A doctor is struggling to diagnose a woman’s flulike illness. She complains of a fever that rises during the day and peaks after dinner (undulant fever), fatigue, spinal tenderness, and loss of appetite. Her lymph nodes are enlarged in physical exam. The doctor has trouble narrowing down the possible etiologies until he hears that the woman","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Streptococcus pneumoniae"},{"label":"B","text":"Pseudomonas aeruginosa"},{"label":"C","text":"Bordetella pertussis"},{"label":"D","text":"Francisella tularensis"},{"label":"E","text":"Brucella species 38 – Miscellaneous Gram-Negative Bacilli"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from stem","whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-ef757050820e","stem":"1) Which of the following is most likely caused by Legionella?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bloody diarrhea"},{"label":"B","text":"Fever lasting less than 24 hours"},{"label":"C","text":"Atypical pneumonia"},{"label":"D","text":"UTI"},{"label":"E","text":"Meningitis"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"provisional_independently_reasoned","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-001194df05e5","stem":"2) Which of the following is the most likely location to find Legionella pneumophila?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Water"},{"label":"B","text":"Soil"},{"label":"C","text":"Food"},{"label":"D","text":"Plants"},{"label":"E","text":"Desert"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-610e4e82957e","stem":"1) What kind of media is most commonly used to grow Legionella?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Chocolate (CHOC)"},{"label":"B","text":"Blood agar plate (BAP)"},{"label":"C","text":"Bile Esculin agar (BEA)"},{"label":"D","text":"MacConkey agar (MAC)"},{"label":"E","text":"Buffered charcoal yeast extract agar (BCYE)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b664b9f1db51","stem":"2) What growth factors are required for Legionella?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Heme (X)"},{"label":"B","text":"NAD (V)"},{"label":"C","text":"Heme and NAD (X and V)"},{"label":"D","text":"Cysteine and iron"},{"label":"E","text":"Cysteine and heme (X)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[],"manualEdits":{}},{"id":"q-a08a3c21ecdc","stem":"3) Which of the following laboratory tests for Legionella uses indirect fluorescent antibody (IFA)?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Culture"},{"label":"B","text":"Urine antigen test"},{"label":"C","text":"Nucleic acid amplification assay"},{"label":"D","text":"Serology"},{"label":"E","text":"Identification (microscopy) Match the following clinical illness with the organism:"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Immunology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-420cd8d204bb","stem":"Which of the following is NOT true (in general) for Clostridium?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gram-negative"},{"label":"B","text":"Bacilli shaped"},{"label":"C","text":"Spore-forming"},{"label":"D","text":"Obligate anaerobes"},{"label":"E","text":"Unable to reduce sulfate to sulfite"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0fa3c34a9a66","stem":"1) A teenage girl enters the emergency room suffering painful muscle spasms. Throughout her examination, she sustains a facial sneer, a stiff arched back, and clamped palms. Her father is anxious about the fact that she has also experienced difficulty eating, probably due to a stiff jaw. The father affirms that her daughter is usually quite active and boasts how, a week ago, she continued a soccer game even after falling on a nail in the field. Which of the following is the most likely cause?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"C. difficile"},{"label":"B","text":"C. perfingens"},{"label":"C","text":"C. septicum"},{"label":"D","text":"C. botulinum"},{"label":"E","text":"C. tetani"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-adf3eafe5ab6","stem":"2) A woman straggles into the emergency room with a marked paralysis of her upper body. She describes the paralysis as a weakness that began in her neck and spread to her arms. She also complains of blurred double vision and requests water to soothe her dry throat. Though she has no fever, she appears quite dizzy and her eyelids are drooping. The day before, she returned from a camping trip where she insists she maintained good hygiene, limiting her diet to canned food only. Which of the following is the most likely cause?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Ophthalmology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"C. difficile"},{"label":"B","text":"C. perfingens"},{"label":"C","text":"C. septicum"},{"label":"D","text":"C. botulinum"},{"label":"E","text":"C. tetani"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Ophthalmology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-947489bf8bc8","stem":"3) An old woman comes to the doctor with a fever and loose bowels. Her diarrhea occurs in tremendous volumes, she complains, though she doesn’t remember seeing blood. She has an unremarkable recent past medical history, except for an infection a few weeks earlier that was treated with clindamycin. Sigmoidoscopy of her colon reveals yellow-white plaques which the doctor predicted after analyzing her stools for toxins. Which of the following is the most likely cause?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"C. difficile"},{"label":"B","text":"C. perfingens"},{"label":"C","text":"C. septicum"},{"label":"D","text":"C. botulinum"},{"label":"E","text":"C. tetani"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-52d147c24af7","stem":"4) A man enters the emergency room claiming to have been stabbed two days earlier. Muscles in his arm hurt, and on palpation small air bubbles are felt below the skin. The wound area exudes a blackish, ill-smelling fluid that generates a crackling sound when touched. The patient has a fever, a low blood pressure, marked tachycardia, and urinated","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Emergency Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"C. difficile"},{"label":"B","text":"C. perfingens"},{"label":"C","text":"C. septicum"},{"label":"D","text":"C. botulinum"},{"label":"E","text":"C. tetani"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Emergency Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from stem","whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-7d046eb37ff8","stem":"5) Which of the following is a cause of nontraumatic myonecrosis and often exists in patients with occult colon cancer, acute leukemia, or diabetes?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"C. difficile"},{"label":"B","text":"C. perfingens"},{"label":"C","text":"C. septicum"},{"label":"D","text":"C. botulinum"},{"label":"E","text":"C. tetani"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3a96d7019c8a","stem":"6) Which of the following is associated with Floppy Baby Syndrome?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"C. difficile"},{"label":"B","text":"C. perfingens"},{"label":"C","text":"C. septicum"},{"label":"D","text":"C. botulinum"},{"label":"E","text":"C. tetani"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f95f6f2b831f","stem":"Which organism is most strongly associated with pseudomembranous colitis?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"C. difficile"},{"label":"B","text":"C. perfringens"},{"label":"C","text":"C. septicum"},{"label":"D","text":"C. botulinum"},{"label":"E","text":"C. tetani"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"independent_checked","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"checked_explained","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[],"manualEdits":[{"field":"stem","original":"7) Which of the following is associated with Pseudomembrane Colitis (PMC)?","corrected":"Which organism is most strongly associated with pseudomembranous colitis?","reason":"language_or_captured_footer_repair"},{"field":"option_B","original":"C. perfingens","corrected":"C. perfringens","reason":"embedded_footer_or_spelling_repair"}]},{"id":"q-3c1871447f0e","stem":"1) Which of the following describes the effect of tetanus toxin?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Unregulated excitatory synaptic activity in the motor neurons"},{"label":"B","text":"Blocks neurotransmission at peripheral cholinergic synapses"},{"label":"C","text":"Induces depolymerization of actin with loss of cellular cytoskeleton"},{"label":"D","text":"Produces chemotaxis; induces cytokine production with hypersecretion of fluid; produces hemorrhagic necrosis"},{"label":"E","text":"C and D"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-134c51ddde81","stem":"2) Which of the following describes the effect of botulinum toxin?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Unregulated excitatory synaptic activity in the motor neurons"},{"label":"B","text":"Blocks neurotransmission at peripheral cholinergic synapses"},{"label":"C","text":"Induces depolymerization of actin with loss of cellular cytoskeleton"},{"label":"D","text":"Produces chemotaxis; induces cytokine production with hypersecretion of fluid; produces hemorrhagic necrosis"},{"label":"E","text":"C and D"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3f7af05850f5","stem":"3) Which of the following describes the effect of C. difficile toxin?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Unregulated excitatory synaptic activity in the motor neurons"},{"label":"B","text":"Blocks neurotransmission at peripheral cholinergic synapses"},{"label":"C","text":"Induces depolymerization of actin with loss of cellular cytoskeleton"},{"label":"D","text":"Produces chemotaxis; induces cytokine production with hypersecretion of fluid; produces hemorrhagic necrosis"},{"label":"E","text":"C and D 41 – Anaerobic, Non Spore Forming, Gram-positive Rods"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"1a5d2be3961120eece2bc317de07c2736183931f"},{"id":"q-0bdb20bf90ca","stem":"1) What is the best description of the shape of Actinomyces?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Coccus"},{"label":"B","text":"Bacillus"},{"label":"C","text":"Spirillum"},{"label":"D","text":"Diplococcus"},{"label":"E","text":"Filamentous"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiolo